Z||000000||walsh2001||04-12-2001||09:20 AM||||Where can I get a new deck lid lock mechanism for my 84 Fiero? I ended up drilling the damn thing out when I locked my keys in the trunk  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||deceler8||04-12-2001||09:39 AM||||People sell these on EBAY all the time.<P>You could also get one from GM.<P>Or you could check the boneyards and you might get lucky. I found one at a boneyard that had the key in it for $1.||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||04-12-2001||04:06 PM||||I just bought one from the Fiero Store for the '87 GT repo I got with only an ignition key. I had to punch the deck lock to start working on it. I bought the door lock kit too. The deck lock was only the lock cylinder and black cover (the part you see sticking out) with an extra chrome one. On mine I have to reuse the rod and spring (rod retainer). The trunk lock as $25 (in a GM box) and the door kit (2 locks + clips) was $22 (Standard Ignition).||||reg||1
